===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something or someone that [[signify|signifies]], makes something more [[significant]] or [[important]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Diane Rubenstein|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=CPzCha2t3csC&pg=PA31&dq=signifier&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwiI84bCg_HKAhVJ2mMKHQcfB_44RhDoAQgrMAM#v=onepage&q=signifier&f=false|title=This is Not a President: Sense, Nonsense, and the American Political Imaginary|passage=If commentators have concurred on the characterization of Reagan as a synecdoche, they have also noted his status as a '''signifier'''.}}
## {{lb|en|cartomancy}} A [[card]] representing a [[querent]], question, or situation.
# {{lb|en|linguistics|philosophy}} A [[sign]], such as a written or spoken [[word]], which [[refer]]s to some concept, object or person, the [[signified]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2001|author=Jonathan Franzen|title=The Corrections
|passage=Here things are getting better and better for women and people of color, and gay men and lesbians, more and more integrated and open, and all you can think about is some stupid, lame problem with '''signifiers''' and signifieds.}}

